Task: Citations from Rust and Swift
Read the original's C and the names the engine's Rust and Swift cite from it

The census needs every function of the original, not just those with a symbol: 1,754 functions the C defines have no symbol of their own (statics the compiler inlined), so a C reader finds the top-level functions, initialised data and macros of source/, skipping comments, literals and other preprocessor lines. 290 definitions without symbols carry a port: comment or 'port' in their name; they are the old hosted port's additions and are set apart, not counted as the original's. The original is then 8,501 functions.

The citations are names of those functions in backticks in a comment of a crate's src/ or of the app's Swift (not tests, not the Swift uniffi generates). 236 are cited today, a superset of the reference map's 159.

